# Review ownership. Required by code-review-gate --architecture-only, which
# resolves the approvers for the architecture layer from this file.
#
# ONE owner, on purpose, and it is a deliberate deviation from the four-eyes
# standing rule — see FRAMEWORK_FEEDBACK.md § FB-005, where it is recorded and
# marked for removal.
#
# GitHub never requests a review from the pull request author (the API rejects
# it with 422 "Review cannot be requested from pull request author"), so a
# single-owner line requests nobody whenever that owner opens the PR. That is
# the intended effect while this project has one available maintainer: the
# review requirement stays declared on the branch, and enforce_admins is false
# so the maintainer can land work.
#
# The previous file listed @MFei8ht and @abecerriltrazodigital so that whoever
# authored a PR, the other was auto-requested. Restore that line — and set
# enforce_admins back to true — the moment a second reviewer is available.
# That is the whole revert.
#
# USER_MANUAL.md § 9.4 declares three architecture-owned paths, not one. The
# tech-stack files are human-owned configuration (AGENTS.md § "Ownership
# boundaries" forbids the agent from editing them), so a change there is an
# architecture decision and needs the same approval as docs/architecture/.
